content.text:
Read ~/Desktop/badges/AGENTS.md first (section 2, rule 10: the Diamond is drawn by the app's gem shader), then the app repo's AGENTS.md in ~/Desktop/screen_time, and follow both. How the gem shader works is in ~/Desktop/screen_time/.claude/plans/2026-10-11-diamond-gem-shader.md and its Progress Log.

Permission: for the Diamond only, you may change the gem shader (ScreenTime/Sources/App/Features/Badges/BadgeGemSurface.metal), the Diamond's model and the 3D badge code in BadgeHeroCard.swift, including the image processing after the render. I, the owner, am asking for this, so the rule that badge agents never edit app code does not apply here. Every other badge must look exactly as it does now. The Diamond work in the repo is new and not committed yet: build on it and never revert it.

Goal: the Diamond should look gorgeous while it just sits on Home, because the stone itself looks better. Today it looks flat and dull at rest, mostly because of a dark bow-tie in the middle. While spinning it looks great: keep the spin at least as good as now. See ~/Downloads/diamond_rest_vs_spin.png and ~/Downloads/diamond_full_turn.mov.

Do this in order:
1. Find the cause of the dark center before changing the look. Make test renders at rest:
   - one with the blue absorption off;
   - one with the light from the 3-bounce shortcut painted a loud color;
   - one showing what the light leaving the middle actually sees.
   Tell me what causes it. If the shortcut or the absorption is a big part of it, fix that first and show the result.
2. Try two or three recuts with a shallower bottom half, closer to the roughly 41 degrees of well-cut diamonds (today it is about 46). Each must still follow rule 10 (convex, flat facets, at most 256 planes, material DiamondGem). Keep the lowest point at the shared float height (Y -2.455) and the width inside the frame. Show each at rest and through the spin, next to today's gem, so I can judge the outline and the spin together.
3. Add star glints last: subtle, camera-style four-point streaks on the brightest compact flashes, coming from the real flashes, never painted. They all point the same way on screen and are completely still at rest. No stars from bright outline pixels. Diamond only. Show two or three strengths.

Don't:
- change the resting angle;
- add lights;
- make anything move or twinkle at rest;
- just make everything brighter.
Placing the studio lights at their real distance is on hold: ask me before trying it.

Limits:
- It must stay smooth on my iPhone 12 mini (the shader is already the heaviest thing on Home), so keep additions cheap.
- No white specks, dots or bright broken lines on the outline at any angle, checked at 4x zoom.
- Never commit, never switch branches.

Deliver, all in ~/Downloads/diamond_codex/:
- app shots at rest of today's Diamond next to each option, at 1x and 4x;
- the side, back and other side poses;
- a slow full-turn video for each finalist;
- the build and test gate results;
- a short report with the cause you found and the option you recommend.
Then stop and wait for my pick. Leave the repo exactly as you found it until I pick, and re-cut the Badges screen picture (BadgeArtDiamond.png) only after I pick.

